    "textsConsentRead": {
      "title": "TextsConsentRead",
      "description": "The newest texts consent row for the recipient's contact that covers the row's business, its business's or every business's (K-05 v1.2 item 28, default 35: by at, a tie to the lower id), as v1.2 gives it (consentId, businessId, revoked and at, unchanged), with two fields more (v1.8, T-1102; README item 47): fromContact, who gave it, and bookingId, the booking it was given for, each read from K-29 v1's own row. Both are optional here only so that every v1.2 to v1.7 answer, which has neither, is a v1.8 answer: a v1.8 call always writes both (textsConsentV1dot8, in sendState.v1dot8Response), and a consumer reads an answer without them as not known, so no yes lifts a stop (T-1099: limit 8's notKnown). A row that withdraws (revoked) is no yes: its fromContact is false, never true, so no reader that skips revoked takes a STOP for the person's own yes (refuse-send-state-stop-read-as-own-yes; README default 82). New in v1.8.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "consentId": {
          "description": "K-29 v1 consents.id.",
          "$ref": "#/$defs/id"
        },
        "businessId": {
          "description": "K-29 v1 consents.business_id: the business the yes is for, or null on a STOP's or a START's row, which covers every business (D102; RULES 7.2, 7.5).",
          "$ref": "#/$defs/nullableId"
        },
        "revoked": {
          "description": "K-29 v1 consents.revoked: true for a row that withdraws (a STOP in any words, or a switch away from this contact: K-29 README, 'Revoked is a row, not an edit').",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "at": {
          "description": "K-29 v1 consents.at: when the yes was given or the stop came.",
          "$ref": "#/$defs/utc"
        },
        "fromContact": {
          "description": "Whether the row is a yes the person sent from the contact it covers, by text (RULES 7.1: 'Never on someone else's word'; RULES 7.5 and S13-32 line 7242: 'from that number'; S13-32 line 7215: 'The business's word counts only for someone who gave the business their number for this booking'). Source (README item 47, default 78): K-29 v1 consents, read with the row, and K-04 v1 turns: true only when revoked is false, channel is text, and either turn_id names a turns row whose handle_id is the row's own handle_id (a turn batches one handle's texts, so a yes given by text in it came from that handle), or turn_id is null and business_id is null (only a STOP's or a START's row may have no business, K-29 consents_every_business_only_texts, and one that does not withdraw is a START, which K-09 v1 records only from the phone's own START text, in its turn or on return by its actor: recordStopOrStart; start-recorded.json). False for every other row: a yes the business entered ('1 Yes' by the owner's text is a turn of the owner's handle; the Today page's is channel page), a page's, an outside AI's or an email's, a yes by text from another handle, a yes no turn wrote that is not a START (README default 79), an email contact's row (default 80), and a row that withdraws (default 82). Reason: limit 8 counts a texts yes newer than the stop as turning texts back on only when it is the person's own word sent from the number that stopped (T-1099; C-125), and v1.2's row could not say who gave it, so every yes read as not known. New in v1.8.",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "bookingId": {
          "description": "The booking the yes was given for: K-29 v1 consents.booking_id as stored (README item 47, default 81): the person's own number given for this booking (RULES 7.1), the terms ticked for it, or a fresh yes on a new booking from that number (RULES 7.5), which turns only that booking's texts back on (S13-32 line 7242); null on a row that names no booking: START's and STOP's rows for every business, and a yes given for the business rather than one booking. Whether that booking was made after the stop is stored nowhere, so it is not read (README default 83, open gap 52). Reason: limit 8 lifts a stop for a row only when the person's own fresh yes names that row's booking (T-1099; C-125). New in v1.8.",
          "$ref": "#/$defs/nullableId"
        }
      },
      "required": ["consentId", "businessId", "revoked", "at"],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "if": {
        "properties": {
          "revoked": {
            "const": true
          }
        }
      },
      "then": {
        "properties": {
          "fromContact": {
            "description": "A row that withdraws is no yes, so it is never the person's own yes (README default 82).",
            "const": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "textsConsentV1dot8": {
      "title": "TextsConsentV1dot8",
      "description": "The texts consent row as a v1.8 call writes it (README item 47): every field of textsConsentRead, by reference, with fromContact and bookingId always stated, never left out, and a row that withdraws never the person's own yes. textsConsentRead takes the two as optional only so that v1.2 to v1.7's answers stay valid; this is the shape a v1.8 producer's answers are checked against (db/repo's sendState), so no consumer meets a v1.8 answer that leaves out who gave a yes or for which booking (refuse-send-state-yes-source-left-out, refuse-send-state-booking-left-out). New in v1.8.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "consentId": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/textsConsentRead/properties/consentId"
        },
        "businessId": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/textsConsentRead/properties/businessId"
        },
        "revoked": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/textsConsentRead/properties/revoked"
        },
        "at": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/textsConsentRead/properties/at"
        },
        "fromContact": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/textsConsentRead/properties/fromContact"
        },
        "bookingId": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/textsConsentRead/properties/bookingId"
        }
      },
      "required": ["consentId", "businessId", "revoked", "at", "fromContact", "bookingId"],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "if": {
        "properties": {
          "revoked": {
            "const": true
          }
        }
      },
      "then": {
        "properties": {
          "fromContact": {
            "description": "A row that withdraws is no yes, so it is never the person's own yes (README default 82).",
            "const": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
