    "sendState.response": {
      "title": "SendStateResponse",
      "description": "What limit 8 reads about a row's recipient, all from one read of the primary (one transaction), as v1.2 answers it (README item 28: each field by reference to v1.2's own definition of it, which v1.3 to v1.7 keep unchanged), with textsConsent's two fields more (v1.8, T-1102; README item 47): fromContact and bookingId, optional here only so that every v1.2 to v1.7 answer is a v1.8 answer. A v1.8 call always writes them (sendState.v1dot8Response). The stopped flag is phone.stopped, K-04 phones.stopped as stored, never derived from textsConsent (STATE note 10; T-1099; README default 84); fromContact and bookingId describe the consent row alone. Limit 8's rules on it, and what each flag holds back, are C-125's.",
